# Workiva MCP server: standing rules

## What we're building
A Python MCP server that exposes the Workiva Public API as tools an AI agent
can call.

## Safety
- Secrets come from .env only (WORKIVA_CLIENT_ID, WORKIVA_CLIENT_SECRET,
  WORKIVA_WORKSPACE_ID). Never print, log, or commit secret values.
- Every write tool refuses to run unless the target workspace equals
  WORKIVA_WORKSPACE_ID (the sandbox lock).
- Never delete anything you didn't create in this session. Record every
  created ID in a run ledger.
- Fake data only. No customer files.

## How to work
- Read the official Public API docs page for an endpoint before calling it.
  Don't guess routes or payloads.
- One step per task. Stop and report when the step's check passes or fails.
- After every write, read the artifact back and compare. A 200/202 response
  is not proof.
- On a timeout or network error, probe the artifact first to see if the write
  landed, then retry. Never blind-retry.
- Check the artifact, not the log, before re-running a partially applied
  step.
- When you learn a platform limit, add it to CAPABILITIES.md with the date
  and how you proved it.
- Every tool is listed in TOOLS.md (name, one line, status: read/write,
  tested Y/N).
- Generated test output goes in outputs/ (gitignored), never committed.
